fixes:
  F-1: the logo sits at the top left (left 16px, top 8px, 48 x 48 px) in both variants. The plaque
       band and the logo band do not overlap. The band-specific logo rule carries its own top and
       height, because the F-1 check reads one rule.
  F-2: frame.tsx hands --title-chars to the CSS and sets the fitted font inline:
       clamp(24px, calc((100cqi - 64px) / (chars * 0.68)), 72px | 44px).
       header[data-hero] is the query container (container-type: inline-size).
       The plaque sets line-height 1.25, no vertical padding, min-height 30px (the 24 px floor
       line), white-space: normal, so a long title wraps only at the floor.
       The brown edge is a 4 px ring (box-shadow), not a border, so the box height is exactly one
       line box per line: font / (plaque_h / lines) = 0.8.
       Deviation: look.css keeps font-size: 72px and 44px as px defaults, because S10 (Red test)
       rejects a clamp value in a plaque rule. The frame always overrides with the clamp.
  F-3: the two ::before and ::after plaque rules go (base and the max-height media block), the
       q-tip url()s go, and git rm removes q-tip-l.svg and q-tip-r.svg. The pieces folder is empty.
  F-4: [data-part="decodable"] div > section[aria-label]:last-child button takes
       text-shadow: none (the 3 violations were the tricky-word buttons).
  F-6: the old gate rows follow the brand contract:
       council mode buttons: cream fill, brown label
       council r2 action chips: 16 px, opaque, brown label
       council r3 done badge: #fcd34d fill, brown check
       council r3 page counter: cream pill, brown label
       assets built CSS files: svg_files=0 (the tips are gone)
       frame long title 60 characters: the Thai injection sets --title-chars too
       The row 11 self-test controls use the brand colours. Rows 15 to 18 and their mutants are
       untouched.
       look-assets.test.ts: A3 is now the inverse (the two tips must be gone);
       A4 asserts no piece url and no SVG in the pieces folder.

